// APW-6 — Net open-count window cap (opens minus completed reviews) — BUGGY variant.
//
// Same intent as the correct variant (at most 3 open PRs at once), but the
// counted events are `response` instead of `request`. A denied open attempt or
// a stalled review then distorts the net open count (opens - reviews), so the
// `< 3` cap is not enforced reliably.
//
// The one-word bug vs. the correct variant: `response` instead of `request`.
//
// Schema: Repo namespace (cap_open_agent_prs_windowed example).
// See: rot/shapes.py (the count-window oracle, build_count_window_ir).
@id("count_window_buggy")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest"::response{} && tp(t))
    ))
    - (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"CompleteReview"::response{} && tp(t))
    )) < 3
};